      <p>The blocks are not identical. Arizona lists a second firm above Kibler Fowler &amp; Cave: Emmy L. Levens, Richard L. Trumka Jr. and Amanda K. Chuzi of Cohen Milstein Sellers &amp; Toll in Washington. West Virginia’s complaint is signed by Christopher D. Pence of Pence Law Firm PLLC in Charleston. Three of his colleagues are listed with him, and the Kibler Fowler &amp; Cave six come after them. West Virginia’s fee request mentions “special assistant attorneys general” but does not say who they are.</p>
      <p>Every filing also lists the state’s own lawyers. Senior Assistant Attorney General Brittany Edwards appears for Arkansas, Assistant Attorney General Sarah M. Dietz signed for Kansas and Brent Mead appears for Montana. Arizona’s block lists John Raymond Dillon IV and Reagan Healey, and West Virginia’s lists four lawyers from the attorney general’s office after the Kibler Fowler &amp; Cave six.</p>
      <p>A signature block names counsel of record. It does not show who wrote a complaint, and none of the sources we reviewed says who wrote these. We did not find the terms of Kibler Fowler &amp; Cave’s engagement with the states, or of the other firms’ engagements, and we did not review the firms’ earlier work for state attorneys general. The eight filings share counsel, and the next section shows that they share text. Shared counsel and shared text did not produce shared conclusions.</p>
